Package: streetlamp
Title: Panel Econometrics for the Effect of Police Stop and Search on
    Recorded Crime
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Mustapha", "Wasseja", , "muswaseja@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Souci", "Frissa", role = "aut"),
    person("Sarah", "Hamed", role = "aut"),
    person("Black Thrive Global", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
  )
Description: Builds an area-by-month panel of recorded crime in England and
    Wales from the data.police.uk bulk archive, attaches stop and search
    intensity as a treatment variable, and provides a panel-econometrics
    toolkit for evaluating policing interventions: two-way fixed effects,
    event studies, difference-in-differences with staggered adoption,
    synthetic control, spatial spillover and displacement models, and
    stop-crime elasticities by offence type. Every panel carries a contract
    recording provenance, coverage, geography vintage and treatment
    definition; every estimator names its identifying assumption and ships
    with a placebo or pre-trend diagnostic.
